000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. SRTMRG.
000300* SORT and MERGE on one SD in one program: a SORT USING and
000400* GIVING puts a file in order, a MERGE joins it with a second
000500* file through an OUTPUT PROCEDURE, and a SORT with the same
000600* OUTPUT PROCEDURE follows, so RETURN serves a sort again after
000700* it served a merge. The sort is IBM's; the merge is the
000800* compiler's. Expected output is worked by hand.
000900 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001000 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001100 FILE-CONTROL.
001200     SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE.
001300     SELECT IN2-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE2.
001400     SELECT W1-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-W1FILE.
001500     SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-SORTWK01.
001600 DATA DIVISION.
001700 FILE SECTION.
001800 FD  IN-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
001900 01  IN-REC PIC X(80).
002000 FD  IN2-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002100 01  IN2-REC PIC X(80).
002200 FD  W1-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002300 01  W1-REC PIC X(80).
002400 SD  SORT-FILE.
002500 01  S-REC.
002600     05  S-KEY    PIC X(5).
002700     05  S-REST   PIC X(75).
002800 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002900 01  SHOWN PIC X(20).
003000 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
003100 MAIN-PARA.
003200     SORT SORT-FILE ASCENDING KEY S-KEY
003300         USING IN-FILE GIVING W1-FILE.
003400     DISPLAY 'MERGE'.
003500     MERGE SORT-FILE ASCENDING KEY S-KEY
003600         USING W1-FILE IN2-FILE OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS SHOW-IT.
003700     DISPLAY 'SORT DESCENDING'.
003800     SORT SORT-FILE DESCENDING KEY S-KEY
003900         USING IN-FILE OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS SHOW-IT.
004000     DISPLAY 'END'.
004100     STOP RUN.
004200 SHOW-IT SECTION.
004300 S1.
004400     RETURN SORT-FILE AT END GO TO S-EXIT.
004500     MOVE S-REC TO SHOWN.
004600     DISPLAY 'RET ' SHOWN.
004700     GO TO S1.
004800 S-EXIT.
004900     EXIT.
